# Inbox -> Assets -> Data Pipeline

- Source materials live in `inbox/<project-slug>/` and stay immutable as raw input.
- Public website files must be copied into `assets/<case-id>/` before linking in `js/data.js`.
- Use one canonical slug per case across folders and data id (`kondi-nova`, `green-park-93`).
- Keep naming stable for media sequences: `after-1`, `after-2`, `before-1`, `compare-1`, `plan`.
- Never reference `inbox` paths from UI code or from `js/data.js`.

## Case Onboarding Steps

- Import inbox photos with `python scripts/process-assets.py --case <id> --from inbox/<slug>/...` (web resize + compress).
- Or optimize files already in `assets/<case-id>/` with `python scripts/process-assets.py --case <id>`.
- Create/update `assets/<case-id>/` with optimized web media only.
- Add one `CASES` entry in `js/data.js` with matching `id` and `cover`.
- Fill `gallery` paths from `assets/<case-id>/...` and verify the files exist.
- If `hasVideo` is true, provide valid `video.fileUrl` and `video.poster`.
- Keep CTA object complete and consistent with other cases.
